---
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
import SectionHeader from "../components/SectionHeader.astro";
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout title="Managed cloud" description="Evaluate the invite-only LiteMCP Composer managed-cloud track, its open-core boundary, current deployment evidence, and the acceptance work that remains before a production service.">
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Managed cloud · Invite only"
    title="An operated-service track for qualified governance pilots."
    description="The current managed-cloud work adds private customer lifecycle, entitlement, billing, support-access, provisioning, and fleet-release controls around the same public product core. It is not represented as generally available or production accepted."
    signal="Pre-1.0 · applications do not create accounts"
  >
    <Fragment slot="actions">
      <a class="button button--primary button--large" href="/design-partners">Apply for a qualified pilot</a>
      <a class="button button--large" href="/docs/getting-started#five-minute-proof">Prove the local product first</a>
    </Fragment>
  </PageHero>

  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="shell">
      <SectionHeader
        eyebrow="Managed cloud contract"
        title="Operated convenience without a self-hosting dependency."
        description="The service composition consumes public LiteMCP packages. Its private control plane may operate customer lifecycle and commercial service concerns, but self-hosting cannot require it, a vendor account, a license server, billing, mandatory telemetry, or call-home."
      />
      <div class="two-column-cards">
        <article>
          <p class="eyebrow">Public product evidence</p>
          <h2>The governance slice runs locally</h2>
          <p>Automated loopback proof covers scoped sessions, filtered discovery, allowed and denied execution, exact-context approval, revocation, audit, and payload-free activation evidence.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <p class="eyebrow">Private service seam</p>
          <h2>Customer operations stay out of the public runtime</h2>
          <p>Qualified intake, account lifecycle, service entitlements, billing records, support grants, provisioning, and fleet rollout belong to the private operated-service boundary.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <p class="eyebrow">Pilot scope</p>
          <h2>One workflow before a broad rollout</h2>
          <p>A design-partner pilot starts with multiple MCP servers, one meaningful identity boundary, one sensitive action, and explicit evidence or privacy acceptance criteria.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <p class="eyebrow">Service discipline</p>
          <h2>Payload-free product analytics</h2>
          <p>The analytics contract excludes tool arguments, tool results, bearer tokens, raw credentials, emails, and display names. Compliance audit remains a separate, redacted evidence path.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section content-section--subtle">
    <div class="shell split-layout">
      <div class="split-layout__aside">
        <p class="eyebrow">Current status</p>
        <h2>An earlier public baseline exists; the current service revision is not production accepted.</h2>
        <p>
          The public origin previously passed site, Worker, TLS, health, readiness, storage-binding,
          authentication-routing, and canonical-domain checks. That evidence predates the current
          managed authority, Insight Plane, and design-partner intake revision and does not prove
          the current end-to-end service.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="legal-note">
        Privileged onboarding, current MCP initialize/list/call, live named-client and identity-provider
        runs, cross-target portability, backup/restore, rollback, load, regional behavior, external
        security review, availability, durability, and support targets remain acceptance work.
        <a href="/design-partners"> Review pilot fit</a> or inspect the
        <a href="https://github.com/reachjalil/liteMCP/blob/main/IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS.md"> implementation evidence ↗</a>.
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
